---
source: crates/holst-cli/src/table.rs
expression: help_of(line)
---
Move a board to the trash, or with --permanently delete it for good. A folder in the trash takes its boards along; a folder deleted for good leaves them in the folder it was in (or the root).
One board to the trash needs no -y. A folder with boards, and --permanently, need -y, since other people lose the boards; without it only the dry run is shown.

USAGE
  holst board rm <board> [flags]

ARGUMENTS
  board   The board or folder to remove

FLAGS
  -w, --workspace ws   Where names are looked up and new things go: a workspace id or part of its name; all of yours by default
      --permanently    Delete for good: a board by its whole name, a folder by id or link
  -y, --yes            Confirm a risky change; without it only the dry run is shown (exit code 77)
  -n, --dry-run        Show what would change; change nothing

INHERITED FLAGS
  --output, --verbose, --base-url, --home, --no-cache, --help   as in `holst -h`

EXAMPLES
  $ holst b rm "Old draft"
  $ holst b rm "Old draft" --permanently -y
  $ holst b rm "Old draft" -n

LEARN MORE
  How a board is given: `holst b -h`.
  Exit codes: `holst help exit-codes`.
